title: what "moving nodes across skgrepos" means
pid: a505f942-62ba-458e-bd8d-00e01013028d
body: |2-
  The user's 'skgconfig.toml' file should list some 'skgrepos'.
  A skgrepo is just a folder on disk.
  Skg lets you keep multiple skgrepos so you can treat them differently
  -- e.g. some of yours might be public, and others private.
  (All of mine are gitrepos, for safety.)

  Moving a node across skgrepos just means
  changing which skgrepo directory holds its file.
  It has to be done *from within the app*.
  If you just move the file, Skg won't know that you did that,
  and its databases will now contain the lie
  that the moved node is in the old place.
